==English==

{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Etruscan_amphora_Louvre_E703_side_B.jpg|thumb|An Etruscan amphora]]

===Etymology===

From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|amphora|||lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἀμφορεύς||vased shaped ornament with a narrow neck|lang=grc|tr=amphoreus|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|amphorae|pl2=amphoras}}
{{wikipedia|amphora}}
{{wikipedia|amphora (unit)}}
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} A two [[handle]]d [[jar]] with a [[narrow]] [[neck]] that was used in [[ancient]] times to store or carry [[wine]] or [[oil]]s.
# One of various units for measuring liquid or volume during the Roman Empire, measuring between 18.5 and 39 [[litre]]s depending on the variant.
# An [[at sign]] (@).

